(1586, 6, '2026-07-09 17:11:55', '2026-07-09 10:11:55', 'Vietnam is one of the world\'s most exciting culinary destinations. From bustling street food markets to family-owned restaurants, every meal tells a story of tradition, culture, and regional flavors.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re visiting Vietnam for the first time, trying authentic Vietnamese cuisine should be at the top of your travel bucket list. Whether you\'re exploring Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Da Nang, Hoi An, Ho Chi Minh City, or the Mekong Delta, you\'ll find unforgettable dishes wherever you go.\r\n\r\nHere\'s our list of the <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam.</b>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li><b> Pho (Vietnamese Noodle Soup) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nNo trip to Vietnam is complete without a bowl of <b>Pho</b>.\r\n\r\nMade with slow-cooked beef or chicken broth, fresh rice noodles, herbs, and tender slices of meat, Pho perfectly represents Vietnamese culinary traditions.\r\n<h3><b>Why You\'ll Love It</b></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich and aromatic broth</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh herbs and lime</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Healthy yet satisfying</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Perfect for breakfast or any time of day</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<b>Best Places</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Hanoi (Northern-style Pho)</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Ho Chi Minh City (Southern-style Pho)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"2\">\r\n 	<li><b> Banh Mi (Vietnamese Sandwich) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOften ranked among the world\'s best sandwiches, Banh Mi combines French influences with authentic Vietnamese ingredients.\r\n\r\nA crispy baguette is filled with grilled pork, chicken, pâté, pickled vegetables, cucumber, herbs, and spicy chili sauce.\r\n<h3>Why It\'s Famous</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Affordable</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Delicious</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Easy to grab on the go</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Available almost everywhere</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"3\">\r\n 	<li><b> Bun Cha </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOriginally from Hanoi, Bun Cha features grilled pork served with rice noodles, fresh herbs, and a flavorful dipping sauce.\r\n\r\nThe smoky grilled meat combined with fresh vegetables creates one of Vietnam\'s most beloved meals.\r\n\r\nPerfect for lunch.\r\n<ol start=\"4\">\r\n 	<li><b> Goi Cuon (Fresh Spring Rolls) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nIf you\'re looking for something healthy, Goi Cuon is the perfect choice.\r\n\r\nFresh shrimp, pork, rice noodles, lettuce, and herbs are wrapped in delicate rice paper and served with peanut dipping sauce.\r\n<h3>Why Tourists Love It</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Low calorie</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Gluten-friendly (depending on sauce)</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Refreshing during hot weather</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"5\">\r\n 	<li><b> Bun Bo Hue </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOriginating from the ancient city of Hue, this spicy beef noodle soup has a stronger flavor than Pho.\r\n\r\nExpect:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich beef broth</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Lemongrass aroma</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Chili oil</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Thick rice noodles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIt\'s ideal for travelers who enjoy bold flavors.\r\n<ol start=\"6\">\r\n 	<li><b> Cao Lau </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOnly truly authentic in Hoi An, Cao Lau combines chewy noodles, roasted pork, herbs, crispy crackers, and a small amount of savory broth.\r\n\r\nMany believe the noodles owe their unique texture to local water sources.\r\n\r\nThis dish cannot be missed if you\'re visiting Central Vietnam.\r\n<ol start=\"7\">\r\n 	<li><b> Com Tam (Broken Rice) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nA signature dish of Southern Vietnam.\r\n\r\nBroken rice is served with grilled pork chops, fried egg, shredded pork skin, pickled vegetables, and fish sauce.\r\n\r\nSimple, filling, and incredibly flavorful.\r\n<ol start=\"8\">\r\n 	<li><b> Banh Xeo (Vietnamese Crispy Pancake) “</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nNamed after the sizzling sound (\"xeo\") made during cooking, this crispy rice pancake is stuffed with shrimp, pork, and bean sprouts.\r\n\r\nWrap each bite with fresh herbs and lettuce before dipping into fish sauce.\r\n\r\nA fun interactive dining experience.\r\n<ol start=\"9\">\r\n 	<li><b> Cha Ca </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nA Hanoi specialty, Cha Ca features turmeric-marinated fish grilled with dill and spring onions.\r\n\r\nServed with rice noodles, peanuts, herbs, and shrimp paste or fish sauce, it offers a unique combination of flavors unlike any other Vietnamese dish.\r\n<ol start=\"10\">\r\n 	<li><b> Egg Coffee (Ca Phe Trung) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nFinish your food adventure with one of Vietnam\'s most iconic drinks.\r\n\r\nEgg Coffee blends strong Vietnamese coffee with whipped egg yolk and condensed milk, creating a creamy dessert-like beverage.\r\n\r\nBest enjoyed in Hanoi\'s traditional cafés.\r\n<h1><b>Tips for First-Time Visitors Trying Vietnamese Food</b></h1>\r\n✔ Eat where local people eat.\r\n\r\n✔ Don\'t be afraid of street food—many vendors have served the same recipes for generations.\r\n\r\n✔ Carry cash, as many small food stalls don\'t accept cards.\r\n\r\n✔ Try regional specialties instead of ordering Pho every day.\r\n\r\n✔ Ask for less chili if you don\'t enjoy spicy food.\r\n\r\n✔ Drink bottled water during your trip.\r\n<h1><b>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</b></h1>\r\n<h3><b>What is the most famous food in Vietnam?</b></h3>\r\nPho is widely recognized as Vietnam\'s national dish and is the most popular choice among international visitors.\r\n<h3><b>Is Vietnamese food spicy?</b></h3>\r\nMost Vietnamese dishes are mildly seasoned. Chili is usually served separately, allowing you to adjust the spice level to your preference.\r\n<h3><b>Is street food safe in Vietnam?</b></h3>\r\nYes, especially when you choose busy vendors with high customer turnover and freshly prepared food.\r\n<h3><b>What is the best Vietnamese food for beginners?</b></h3>\r\nIf it\'s your first visit, start with:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Pho</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Banh Mi</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Goi Cuon</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Bun Cha</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Com Tam</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThese dishes are flavorful, easy to enjoy, and widely available throughout Vietnam.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nVietnam\'s food is much more than a meal—it\'s an unforgettable cultural experience. Every region offers unique specialties shaped by local traditions, fresh ingredients, and centuries of culinary heritage.\r\n\r\nWhether you\'re savoring a steaming bowl of Pho in Hanoi, enjoying a crispy Banh Mi in Hoi An, or tasting Broken Rice in Ho Chi Minh City, each bite brings you closer to understanding Vietnam\'s rich culture.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re planning your first trip, make it your mission to try these <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Foods</b>. Your taste buds will thank you—and you\'ll leave Vietnam with memories as rich as its cuisine.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam | First-Time Food Guide ', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'top-10-vietnamese-food-you-must-try-in-vietnam-first-time-food-guide', '', '', '2026-07-09 17:11:55', '2026-07-09 10:11:55', '', 0, 'https://vionistravel.com/?p=1586', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(1587, 6, '2026-07-09 17:11:53', '2026-07-09 10:11:53', '&nbsp;\n\nVietnam is one of the world\'s most exciting culinary destinations. From bustling street food markets to family-owned restaurants, every meal tells a story of tradition, culture, and regional flavors.\n\nIf you\'re visiting Vietnam for the first time, trying authentic Vietnamese cuisine should be at the top of your travel bucket list. Whether you\'re exploring Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Da Nang, Hoi An, Ho Chi Minh City, or the Mekong Delta, you\'ll find unforgettable dishes wherever you go.\n\nHere\'s our list of the <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam.</b>\n<ol>\n 	<li><b> Pho (Vietnamese Noodle Soup) </b></li>\n</ol>\nNo trip to Vietnam is complete without a bowl of <b>Pho</b>.\n\nMade with slow-cooked beef or chicken broth, fresh rice noodles, herbs, and tender slices of meat, Pho perfectly represents Vietnamese culinary traditions.\n<h3><b>Why You\'ll Love It</b></h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich and aromatic broth</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh herbs and lime</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Healthy yet satisfying</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Perfect for breakfast or any time of day</li>\n</ul>\n<b>Best Places</b>\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Hanoi (Northern-style Pho)</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Ho Chi Minh City (Southern-style Pho)</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n 	<li><b> Banh Mi (Vietnamese Sandwich) </b></li>\n</ol>\nOften ranked among the world\'s best sandwiches, Banh Mi combines French influences with authentic Vietnamese ingredients.\n\nA crispy baguette is filled with grilled pork, chicken, pâté, pickled vegetables, cucumber, herbs, and spicy chili sauce.\n<h3>Why It\'s Famous</h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Affordable</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Delicious</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Easy to grab on the go</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Available almost everywhere</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n 	<li><b> Bun Cha </b></li>\n</ol>\nOriginally from Hanoi, Bun Cha features grilled pork served with rice noodles, fresh herbs, and a flavorful dipping sauce.\n\nThe smoky grilled meat combined with fresh vegetables creates one of Vietnam\'s most beloved meals.\n\nPerfect for lunch.\n<ol start=\"4\">\n 	<li><b> Goi Cuon (Fresh Spring Rolls) </b></li>\n</ol>\nIf you\'re looking for something healthy, Goi Cuon is the perfect choice.\n\nFresh shrimp, pork, rice noodles, lettuce, and herbs are wrapped in delicate rice paper and served with peanut dipping sauce.\n<h3>Why Tourists Love It</h3>\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Low calorie</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Gluten-friendly (depending on sauce)</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Refreshing during hot weather</li>\n</ul>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n 	<li><b> Bun Bo Hue </b></li>\n</ol>\nOriginating from the ancient city of Hue, this spicy beef noodle soup has a stronger flavor than Pho.\n\nExpect:\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich beef broth</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Lemongrass aroma</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Chili oil</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Thick rice noodles</li>\n</ul>\nIt\'s ideal for travelers who enjoy bold flavors.\n<ol start=\"6\">\n 	<li><b> Cao Lau </b></li>\n</ol>\nOnly truly authentic in Hoi An, Cao Lau combines chewy noodles, roasted pork, herbs, crispy crackers, and a small amount of savory broth.\n\nMany believe the noodles owe their unique texture to local water sources.\n\nThis dish cannot be missed if you\'re visiting Central Vietnam.\n<ol start=\"7\">\n 	<li><b> Com Tam (Broken Rice) </b></li>\n</ol>\nA signature dish of Southern Vietnam.\n\nBroken rice is served with grilled pork chops, fried egg, shredded pork skin, pickled vegetables, and fish sauce.\n\nSimple, filling, and incredibly flavorful.\n<ol start=\"8\">\n 	<li><b> Banh Xeo (Vietnamese Crispy Pancake) “</b></li>\n</ol>\nNamed after the sizzling sound (\"xeo\") made during cooking, this crispy rice pancake is stuffed with shrimp, pork, and bean sprouts.\n\nWrap each bite with fresh herbs and lettuce before dipping into fish sauce.\n\nA fun interactive dining experience.\n<ol start=\"9\">\n 	<li><b> Cha Ca </b></li>\n</ol>\nA Hanoi specialty, Cha Ca features turmeric-marinated fish grilled with dill and spring onions.\n\nServed with rice noodles, peanuts, herbs, and shrimp paste or fish sauce, it offers a unique combination of flavors unlike any other Vietnamese dish.\n<ol start=\"10\">\n 	<li><b> Egg Coffee (Ca Phe Trung) </b></li>\n</ol>\nFinish your food adventure with one of Vietnam\'s most iconic drinks.\n\nEgg Coffee blends strong Vietnamese coffee with whipped egg yolk and condensed milk, creating a creamy dessert-like beverage.\n\nBest enjoyed in Hanoi\'s traditional cafés.\n<h1><b>Tips for First-Time Visitors Trying Vietnamese Food</b></h1>\n✔ Eat where local people eat.\n\n✔ Don\'t be afraid of street food—many vendors have served the same recipes for generations.\n\n✔ Carry cash, as many small food stalls don\'t accept cards.\n\n✔ Try regional specialties instead of ordering Pho every day.\n\n✔ Ask for less chili if you don\'t enjoy spicy food.\n\n✔ Drink bottled water during your trip.\n<h1><b>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</b></h1>\n<h3><b>What is the most famous food in Vietnam?</b></h3>\nPho is widely recognized as Vietnam\'s national dish and is the most popular choice among international visitors.\n<h3><b>Is Vietnamese food spicy?</b></h3>\nMost Vietnamese dishes are mildly seasoned. Chili is usually served separately, allowing you to adjust the spice level to your preference.\n<h3><b>Is street food safe in Vietnam?</b></h3>\nYes, especially when you choose busy vendors with high customer turnover and freshly prepared food.\n<h3><b>What is the best Vietnamese food for beginners?</b></h3>\nIf it\'s your first visit, start with:\n<ul>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Pho</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Banh Mi</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Goi Cuon</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Bun Cha</li>\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Com Tam</li>\n</ul>\nThese dishes are flavorful, easy to enjoy, and widely available throughout Vietnam.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nVietnam\'s food is much more than a meal—it\'s an unforgettable cultural experience. Every region offers unique specialties shaped by local traditions, fresh ingredients, and centuries of culinary heritage.\n\nWhether you\'re savoring a steaming bowl of Pho in Hanoi, enjoying a crispy Banh Mi in Hoi An, or tasting Broken Rice in Ho Chi Minh City, each bite brings you closer to understanding Vietnam\'s rich culture.\n\nIf you\'re planning your first trip, make it your mission to try these <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Foods</b>. Your taste buds will thank you—and you\'ll leave Vietnam with memories as rich as its cuisine.\n\n&nbsp;', 'Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam | First-Time Food Guide ', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1586-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-09 17:11:53', '2026-07-09 10:11:53', '', 1586, 'https://vionistravel.com/?p=1587', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(1588, 6, '2026-07-09 17:11:55', '2026-07-09 10:11:55', 'Vietnam is one of the world\'s most exciting culinary destinations. From bustling street food markets to family-owned restaurants, every meal tells a story of tradition, culture, and regional flavors.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re visiting Vietnam for the first time, trying authentic Vietnamese cuisine should be at the top of your travel bucket list. Whether you\'re exploring Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Da Nang, Hoi An, Ho Chi Minh City, or the Mekong Delta, you\'ll find unforgettable dishes wherever you go.\r\n\r\nHere\'s our list of the <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam.</b>\r\n<ol>\r\n 	<li><b> Pho (Vietnamese Noodle Soup) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nNo trip to Vietnam is complete without a bowl of <b>Pho</b>.\r\n\r\nMade with slow-cooked beef or chicken broth, fresh rice noodles, herbs, and tender slices of meat, Pho perfectly represents Vietnamese culinary traditions.\r\n<h3><b>Why You\'ll Love It</b></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich and aromatic broth</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh herbs and lime</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Healthy yet satisfying</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Perfect for breakfast or any time of day</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<b>Best Places</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Hanoi (Northern-style Pho)</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Ho Chi Minh City (Southern-style Pho)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"2\">\r\n 	<li><b> Banh Mi (Vietnamese Sandwich) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOften ranked among the world\'s best sandwiches, Banh Mi combines French influences with authentic Vietnamese ingredients.\r\n\r\nA crispy baguette is filled with grilled pork, chicken, pâté, pickled vegetables, cucumber, herbs, and spicy chili sauce.\r\n<h3>Why It\'s Famous</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Affordable</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Delicious</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Easy to grab on the go</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Available almost everywhere</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"3\">\r\n 	<li><b> Bun Cha </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOriginally from Hanoi, Bun Cha features grilled pork served with rice noodles, fresh herbs, and a flavorful dipping sauce.\r\n\r\nThe smoky grilled meat combined with fresh vegetables creates one of Vietnam\'s most beloved meals.\r\n\r\nPerfect for lunch.\r\n<ol start=\"4\">\r\n 	<li><b> Goi Cuon (Fresh Spring Rolls) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nIf you\'re looking for something healthy, Goi Cuon is the perfect choice.\r\n\r\nFresh shrimp, pork, rice noodles, lettuce, and herbs are wrapped in delicate rice paper and served with peanut dipping sauce.\r\n<h3>Why Tourists Love It</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Fresh</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Low calorie</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Gluten-friendly (depending on sauce)</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Refreshing during hot weather</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol start=\"5\">\r\n 	<li><b> Bun Bo Hue </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOriginating from the ancient city of Hue, this spicy beef noodle soup has a stronger flavor than Pho.\r\n\r\nExpect:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Rich beef broth</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Lemongrass aroma</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Chili oil</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Thick rice noodles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nIt\'s ideal for travelers who enjoy bold flavors.\r\n<ol start=\"6\">\r\n 	<li><b> Cao Lau </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nOnly truly authentic in Hoi An, Cao Lau combines chewy noodles, roasted pork, herbs, crispy crackers, and a small amount of savory broth.\r\n\r\nMany believe the noodles owe their unique texture to local water sources.\r\n\r\nThis dish cannot be missed if you\'re visiting Central Vietnam.\r\n<ol start=\"7\">\r\n 	<li><b> Com Tam (Broken Rice) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nA signature dish of Southern Vietnam.\r\n\r\nBroken rice is served with grilled pork chops, fried egg, shredded pork skin, pickled vegetables, and fish sauce.\r\n\r\nSimple, filling, and incredibly flavorful.\r\n<ol start=\"8\">\r\n 	<li><b> Banh Xeo (Vietnamese Crispy Pancake) “</b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nNamed after the sizzling sound (\"xeo\") made during cooking, this crispy rice pancake is stuffed with shrimp, pork, and bean sprouts.\r\n\r\nWrap each bite with fresh herbs and lettuce before dipping into fish sauce.\r\n\r\nA fun interactive dining experience.\r\n<ol start=\"9\">\r\n 	<li><b> Cha Ca </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nA Hanoi specialty, Cha Ca features turmeric-marinated fish grilled with dill and spring onions.\r\n\r\nServed with rice noodles, peanuts, herbs, and shrimp paste or fish sauce, it offers a unique combination of flavors unlike any other Vietnamese dish.\r\n<ol start=\"10\">\r\n 	<li><b> Egg Coffee (Ca Phe Trung) </b></li>\r\n</ol>\r\nFinish your food adventure with one of Vietnam\'s most iconic drinks.\r\n\r\nEgg Coffee blends strong Vietnamese coffee with whipped egg yolk and condensed milk, creating a creamy dessert-like beverage.\r\n\r\nBest enjoyed in Hanoi\'s traditional cafés.\r\n<h1><b>Tips for First-Time Visitors Trying Vietnamese Food</b></h1>\r\n✔ Eat where local people eat.\r\n\r\n✔ Don\'t be afraid of street food—many vendors have served the same recipes for generations.\r\n\r\n✔ Carry cash, as many small food stalls don\'t accept cards.\r\n\r\n✔ Try regional specialties instead of ordering Pho every day.\r\n\r\n✔ Ask for less chili if you don\'t enjoy spicy food.\r\n\r\n✔ Drink bottled water during your trip.\r\n<h1><b>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</b></h1>\r\n<h3><b>What is the most famous food in Vietnam?</b></h3>\r\nPho is widely recognized as Vietnam\'s national dish and is the most popular choice among international visitors.\r\n<h3><b>Is Vietnamese food spicy?</b></h3>\r\nMost Vietnamese dishes are mildly seasoned. Chili is usually served separately, allowing you to adjust the spice level to your preference.\r\n<h3><b>Is street food safe in Vietnam?</b></h3>\r\nYes, especially when you choose busy vendors with high customer turnover and freshly prepared food.\r\n<h3><b>What is the best Vietnamese food for beginners?</b></h3>\r\nIf it\'s your first visit, start with:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Pho</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Banh Mi</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Goi Cuon</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Bun Cha</li>\r\n 	<li aria-level=\"1\">Com Tam</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThese dishes are flavorful, easy to enjoy, and widely available throughout Vietnam.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nVietnam\'s food is much more than a meal—it\'s an unforgettable cultural experience. Every region offers unique specialties shaped by local traditions, fresh ingredients, and centuries of culinary heritage.\r\n\r\nWhether you\'re savoring a steaming bowl of Pho in Hanoi, enjoying a crispy Banh Mi in Hoi An, or tasting Broken Rice in Ho Chi Minh City, each bite brings you closer to understanding Vietnam\'s rich culture.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re planning your first trip, make it your mission to try these <b>Top 10 Vietnamese Foods</b>. Your taste buds will thank you—and you\'ll leave Vietnam with memories as rich as its cuisine.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;', 'Top 10 Vietnamese Food You Must Try in Vietnam | First-Time Food Guide ', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1586-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-09 17:11:55', '2026-07-09 10:11:55', '', 1586, 'https://vionistravel.com/?p=1588', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(1589, 6, '2026-07-09 17:12:38', '2026-07-09 10:12:38', '<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Vietnam is famous for iconic destinations like Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Hoi An, and Ho Chi Minh City. But beyond these well-known attractions lies another side of the country—one filled with untouched beaches, hidden waterfalls, remote mountain villages, pristine islands, and breathtaking landscapes that many travelers never get to experience.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\'re looking to escape the crowds and discover authentic Vietnam, these hidden gems deserve a place on your itinerary.</span>\r\n<h1><b>1. Pu Luong Nature Reserve</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located just a few hours from Hanoi, Pu Luong is often described as a quieter alternative to Sapa.</span>\r\n<h3><b>Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Endless rice terraces</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional Thai ethnic villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bamboo water wheels</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Peaceful hiking trails</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eco-lodges surrounded by mountains</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best for:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nature lovers, photographers, and slow travelers.</span>\r\n<h1><b>2. Bai Xep Beach (Quy Nhon)</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unlike Vietnam\'s more famous beaches, Bai Xep remains peaceful and uncrowded.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Expect:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crystal-clear water</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Golden sand</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Local fishing boats</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Relaxed atmosphere</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Perfect for travelers seeking tranquility.</span>\r\n<h1><b>3. Ha Giang Loop</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Although becoming increasingly popular among adventure travelers, Ha Giang still feels wonderfully untouched.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Spectacular mountain passes</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone peaks</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional ethnic villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Local markets</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scenic motorbike routes</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many visitors consider Ha Giang the most beautiful region in Vietnam.</span>\r\n<h1><b>4. Ba Be Lake</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nestled within Ba Be National Park, this is Vietnam\'s largest natural freshwater lake.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Activities include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Kayaking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Boat tours</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Jungle trekking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cave exploration</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Homestays with local families</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\'s an excellent destination for eco-tourism.</span>\r\n<h1><b>5. Ly Son Island</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Often called Vietnam\'s \"Kingdom of Garlic,\" Ly Son Island offers volcanic landscapes unlike anywhere else in the country.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don\'t miss:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To Vo Gate</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hang Pagoda</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coastal viewpoints</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The island remains relatively undiscovered by international tourists.</span>\r\n<h1><b>6. Phong Nha\'s Hidden Caves</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most travelers visit the famous caves, but the surrounding region offers many lesser-known adventures.</span>\r\n\r\n<i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Phong Nha Cave Vietnam is one of the most wonderful caves in the world (Source: Collected)</span></i>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explore:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Jungle trekking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Secret cave systems</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Underground rivers</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wildlife encounters</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rural villages</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Adventure enthusiasts will love the variety of outdoor experiences.</span>\r\n<h1><b>7. Kon Tum</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located in Vietnam\'s Central Highlands, Kon Tum is rich in indigenous culture and natural beauty.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional Rong houses</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wooden Cathedral</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coffee plantations</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Suspension bridges</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ethnic minority villages</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A fascinating destination for cultural travelers.</span>\r\n<h1><b>8. Con Dao Islands</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Far less crowded than Phu Quoc, Con Dao combines pristine beaches with remarkable history.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Visitors enjoy:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Turtle nesting season</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Diving and snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Luxury resorts</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crystal-clear water</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">National park hiking</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nature lovers will appreciate the island\'s protected ecosystems.</span>\r\n<h1><b>9. Tuy Hoa (Phu Yen)</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Phu Yen remains one of Vietnam\'s most underrated coastal provinces.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Top attractions:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ganh Da Dia (Basalt Cliffs)</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bai Mon Beach</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mui Dien Lighthouse</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Quiet fishing villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood markets</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The dramatic coastline offers incredible sunrise views.</span>\r\n<h1><b>10. Cat Ba National Park</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While many tourists only cruise through Ha Long Bay, few spend enough time exploring Cat Ba Island.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Discover:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dense tropical forests</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone mountains</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hidden beaches</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hiking trails</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wildlife conservation areas</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\'s an excellent destination for outdoor enthusiasts.</span>\r\n<h1><b>11. Cham Islands</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located off the coast of Hoi An, the Cham Islands are part of a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Popular activities include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scuba diving</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coral reef exploration</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Seafood dining</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Island hopping</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The marine biodiversity is among Vietnam\'s finest.</span>\r\n<h1><b>12. Ban Gioc Waterfall</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located on Vietnam\'s northern border, Ban Gioc is one of Southeast Asia\'s most spectacular waterfalls.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Massive cascading waterfalls</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bamboo raft rides</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone mountains</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Quiet countryside</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Stunning photography opportunities</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Despite its beauty, it remains one of Vietnam\'s least-visited natural wonders.</span>', 'Hidden Gems in Vietnam: 12 Secret Places You Should Visit Beyond the Tourist Trail ', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'hidden-gems-in-vietnam', '', '', '2026-07-09 17:19:46', '2026-07-09 10:19:46', '', 0, 'https://vionistravel.com/?p=1589', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(1590, 6, '2026-07-09 17:12:38', '2026-07-09 10:12:38', '&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<b>SEO URL:</b>\r\n\r\n<b>/hidden-gems-in-vietnam</b><b> </b>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Vietnam is famous for iconic destinations like Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Hoi An, and Ho Chi Minh City. But beyond these well-known attractions lies another side of the country—one filled with untouched beaches, hidden waterfalls, remote mountain villages, pristine islands, and breathtaking landscapes that many travelers never get to experience.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\'re looking to escape the crowds and discover authentic Vietnam, these hidden gems deserve a place on your itinerary.</span>\r\n<h1><b>1. Pu Luong Nature Reserve</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located just a few hours from Hanoi, Pu Luong is often described as a quieter alternative to Sapa.</span>\r\n<h3><b>Highlights</b></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Endless rice terraces</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional Thai ethnic villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bamboo water wheels</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Peaceful hiking trails</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eco-lodges surrounded by mountains</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Best for:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nature lovers, photographers, and slow travelers.</span>\r\n<h1><b>2. Bai Xep Beach (Quy Nhon)</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Unlike Vietnam\'s more famous beaches, Bai Xep remains peaceful and uncrowded.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Expect:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crystal-clear water</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Golden sand</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Local fishing boats</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Relaxed atmosphere</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Perfect for travelers seeking tranquility.</span>\r\n<h1><b>3. Ha Giang Loop</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Although becoming increasingly popular among adventure travelers, Ha Giang still feels wonderfully untouched.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Spectacular mountain passes</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone peaks</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional ethnic villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Local markets</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scenic motorbike routes</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many visitors consider Ha Giang the most beautiful region in Vietnam.</span>\r\n<h1><b>4. Ba Be Lake</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nestled within Ba Be National Park, this is Vietnam\'s largest natural freshwater lake.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Activities include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Kayaking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Boat tours</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Jungle trekking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cave exploration</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Homestays with local families</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\'s an excellent destination for eco-tourism.</span>\r\n<h1><b>5. Ly Son Island</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Often called Vietnam\'s \"Kingdom of Garlic,\" Ly Son Island offers volcanic landscapes unlike anywhere else in the country.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Don\'t miss:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To Vo Gate</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hang Pagoda</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coastal viewpoints</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The island remains relatively undiscovered by international tourists.</span>\r\n<h1><b>6. Phong Nha\'s Hidden Caves</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most travelers visit the famous caves, but the surrounding region offers many lesser-known adventures.</span>\r\n\r\n<i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Phong Nha Cave Vietnam is one of the most wonderful caves in the world (Source: Collected)</span></i>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Explore:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Jungle trekking</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Secret cave systems</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Underground rivers</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wildlife encounters</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rural villages</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Adventure enthusiasts will love the variety of outdoor experiences.</span>\r\n<h1><b>7. Kon Tum</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located in Vietnam\'s Central Highlands, Kon Tum is rich in indigenous culture and natural beauty.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traditional Rong houses</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wooden Cathedral</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coffee plantations</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Suspension bridges</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ethnic minority villages</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A fascinating destination for cultural travelers.</span>\r\n<h1><b>8. Con Dao Islands</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Far less crowded than Phu Quoc, Con Dao combines pristine beaches with remarkable history.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Visitors enjoy:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Turtle nesting season</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Diving and snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Luxury resorts</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Crystal-clear water</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">National park hiking</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Nature lovers will appreciate the island\'s protected ecosystems.</span>\r\n<h1><b>9. Tuy Hoa (Phu Yen)</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Phu Yen remains one of Vietnam\'s most underrated coastal provinces.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Top attractions:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ganh Da Dia (Basalt Cliffs)</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bai Mon Beach</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mui Dien Lighthouse</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Quiet fishing villages</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fresh seafood markets</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The dramatic coastline offers incredible sunrise views.</span>\r\n<h1><b>10. Cat Ba National Park</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While many tourists only cruise through Ha Long Bay, few spend enough time exploring Cat Ba Island.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Discover:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dense tropical forests</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone mountains</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hidden beaches</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hiking trails</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Wildlife conservation areas</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\'s an excellent destination for outdoor enthusiasts.</span>\r\n<h1><b>11. Cham Islands</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located off the coast of Hoi An, the Cham Islands are part of a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Popular activities include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Snorkeling</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scuba diving</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Coral reef exploration</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Seafood dining</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Island hopping</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The marine biodiversity is among Vietnam\'s finest.</span>\r\n<h1><b>12. Ban Gioc Waterfall</b></h1>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Located on Vietnam\'s northern border, Ban Gioc is one of Southeast Asia\'s most spectacular waterfalls.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Highlights include:</span>\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Massive cascading waterfalls</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bamboo raft rides</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Limestone mountains</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Quiet countryside</span></li>\r\n 	<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Stunning photography opportunities</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Despite its beauty, it remains one of Vietnam\'s least-visited natural wonders.</span>', 'Hidden Gems in Vietnam: 12 Secret Places You Should Visit Beyond the Tourist Trail ', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '1589-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-07-09 17:12:38', '2026-07-09 10:12:38', '', 1589, 'https://vionistravel.com/?p=1590', 0, 'revision', '', 0);
